 "narration": [
  "Most people switch on the AC and drop it straight to eighteen. Here's why that's costing you.",
  "Since January 2020, star-labelled room ACs sold in India must ship with a default setting of 24 degrees.",
  "That's not random. The Bureau of Energy Efficiency estimated that moving from 20 to 24 degrees can cut an AC's electricity use by about 24 percent.",
  "And setting it colder doesn't cool the room any faster. The AC just keeps running longer, chasing a colder target.",
  "So start at 24. Switch on the ceiling fan, and close the curtains on the sunny side.",
  "In summer, clean the filters every few weeks, and get the unit serviced before the heat arrives.",
  "Twenty-four isn't about being uncomfortable. It's about paying only for the cooling you actually feel."
